---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';
---
<Base title="About" description={SITE.tagline}>
  <div class="wrap">
  <header class="page-head"><h1>About</h1></header>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>I build AI systems, prove they work, and show other engineers how to build them too. My work spans hands-on engineering, technical leadership and customer-facing solution architecture.</p>
    <p>At SalesAi, I lead emerging technology and the AI Center of Practice. I have built a custom model for phone conversations, speech integrations on Google Cloud L4 GPUs, an agent evaluation harness, a customer-data LoRA fine-tuning pipeline, social communication agents and LiveKit voice agents. I designed and led the move from a white-label voice service to our own agent harness using Whisper, Gemini, ElevenLabs, Twilio SIP and GCP. This company work is described here, not published as open source.</p>
    <p>My independent work is public. I published a <a href="/projects/five-lane-router">request router</a> with its model, dataset, evaluation and a <a href="https://huggingface.co/blog/ericmey/train-your-own-request-router">step-by-step tutorial</a>. I built <a href="/projects/musubi">Musubi</a>, shared memory infrastructure for AI agents, and a <a href="/projects/musubi-ecosystem">family of host plugins</a> that bring it into the tools people already use.</p>
    <p>Before this, I led product engineering at SalesAi and engineering teams at Salesforce. I managed Salesforce's internal Slack engineering team and its integration of Einstein AI into internal tools. Earlier work includes software for county governments and my own consultancy.</p>
    <p>I work in Python, TypeScript, JavaScript, Java and C, across models, APIs, hardware and deployment. Outside of work: guitar, sound design and custom music hardware.</p>
    <p>Based in {SITE.location}. I work remotely and can travel. <a href={`mailto:${SITE.links.email}`}>Email me</a> or find me on <a href={SITE.links.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a>.</p>
  </div>
  </div>
</Base>
